"""Render the execution report from actual pixel, oracle, browser and preservation receipts."""
import json
import math
import statistics
from phase9_contract import ROOT,OUT,sha
def read(name):return json.loads((OUT/name).read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
def run():
    a=read('TRIANGULAR_ANALYSIS.json');o=read('INDEPENDENT_VALIDATION.json');c=read('ANALYSIS_CONTRACT.json');q=read('SOURCE_QUALIFICATION.json');v=read('VISUAL_AND_PERFORMANCE.json');p=read('PRESERVATION.json');m=read('RUNTIME_MEMORY.json');t=read('full-browser-results.json');assert t['stats']['expected']==111 and t['stats']['unexpected']==0
    assert (OUT/'POSITIVE_FULL_EVIDENCE.csv').is_file()
    pixels=a['pixels'];s=pixels[0]['scan'];unique_wrong=math.fsum(set(r['frp_mw'] for r in pixels))
    lines=['# Phase 9 — triangular sensor continuity execution','',
    'Client date: 2026-11-14. **The sixteen-pixel same-platform investigation is implemented and independently recounted. Qualified shared observation support remains UNKNOWN; no calibration or generalized historical continuity has been demonstrated. G4: ADJUSTMENT_WITHHELD.**','',
    '## Measured answer','',
    'All sixteen VIIRS 375 m positives belong to scan27, with the same scan interval as their nearest VIIRS750m centers. The exact fire-file metadata names the same M13 radiance input, `'+a['same_named_M13_input']+'`, in both products. All relevant stored orbit-midpoint vectors also agree exactly. Thus different named M13 input granules or different scan intervals are not the explanation for these candidate associations. Exact pixel exposure times and physical containment are not established.','',
    'All sixteen nearest750m centers have native mask5 and raw QA2; these are not qualified non-detections at the375m locations. The375m and750m products use different detection algorithms, bands and production versions. The evidence is consistent with a product-response difference, but does not isolate spatial resolution, algorithm thresholds, processing vintage, cloud effects or geolocation uncertainty as the cause.','',
    'The 375 m algorithm can use M13 radiance to estimate FRP even when the separate VNP14 detection algorithm does not output a positive at the candidate750m index. A375m M13-based FRP allocation is not itself a positive VNP14 fire retrieval. Twelve allocation-consistent index/radiance groups comprise eight singletons and four pairs. Every pair has equal M13/background radiance and equal fractional FRP. All sixteen native row/sample addresses and geolocations are distinct; none is marked residual bowtie.','',
    f"Summing each allocated native fraction once gives **{a['allocated_frp_sum_mw']:.11f} MW** (22.37MW rounded). Deduplicating equal fractions would incorrectly yield {unique_wrong:.11f} MW. Adding reconstructed group totals to their constituent fractions would double-count. These are not16 independent FRP measurements,12 independent events, physical fire counts, burned area, event energy or biomass loss. The allocation-group interpretation is supported by the guide and actual radiance/fraction repetition; it is not independently verified physical pixel containment.",'',
    '## Fixed follow-up and exact inputs','',
    f"`phase9/ANALYSIS_CONTRACT.json`, SHA256 `{sha(OUT/'ANALYSIS_CONTRACT.json')}`, froze all16 known Phase8 positives and the same six inputs before new pixel-level/group analysis. This is a disclosed follow-up to a known16/0/0 result, not a blind calibration sample. The Phase8 AOI `[-117.2,54.75,-116.4,55.0]` and parent contract, datasets and outcomes remain unchanged. No replacement event, new raw science payload or holdout evaluation was used.",'',
    'The candidate rule is an exhaustive WGS84 geodesic nearest-center search over the fixed AOI plus0.05° halo, with row/sample tie breaks. An independent implementation uses scalar Vincenty rather than production PROJ Geod. The floor(row/2),floor(column/2) index hypothesis was tested after geolocation-based association: all16 happen to agree. This tests a center association; it never assumes four-to-one physical containment.','',
    '| Exact original NASA input | SHA256 |','|---|---|']
    for product,r in a['input_receipts'].items():lines.append(f"| {product}: [{r['file'].split('/')[-1]}]({r['url']}) | `{r['sha256']}` |")
    lines+=['', 'All six original payload hashes were reverified. Exact fire-to-geolocation input identities and internal payload IDs remain supported by the unchanged Phase8 manifests and independent provenance checks. The named common M13 input has not been independently downloaded/hashed in Phase9; the metadata-name agreement is not a claim of bit-identical processing through both fire algorithms. New science payload bytes:0. The new public CMR collection metadata response is18,618 bytes, SHA256 `'+q['CMR_collection']['sha256']+'`; no authenticated request was needed.','',
    '## Complete sixteen-pixel evidence','',
    f"Every row has native mask8/confidence8; nominal375m input bits0–6; geolocation flag0; cloud adjacency0; water adjacency0; residual bowtie false; duplicate native address false; duplicate center false. All reported FRP values are finite and positive. Physical scan/track dimensions are UNKNOWN, not assigned nominal375m rectangles. Every375m row uses granule `{pixels[0]['granule']}` and scan{ s['id']}, bounded by `{s['start_utc']}`–`{s['end_utc']}`. The750m candidate scan intervals are identical. Those are complete-scan bounds, not exact per-pixel exposure times.",'',
    '| ID |375m row,col | Latitude, longitude | Raw375m QA | Allocated MW |750m row,col |750m mask / QA | Center distance m |','|---|---|---|---:|---:|---|---|---:|']
    for r in pixels:
        n=r['viirs750'];lines.append(f"| {r['id']} | {r['row']},{r['col']} | {r['lat']:.8f}, {r['lon']:.8f} | {r['raw_qa']} | {r['frp_mw']:.9f} | {n['row']},{n['col']} | {n['mask']} / {n['qa']} | {n['distance_m']:.4f} |")
    lines+=['', '`phase9/POSITIVE_FULL_EVIDENCE.csv` is the actual tested browser export: all16 rows with scan UTC, confidence, every applicable375m QA bit, cloud/water adjacency, geolocation flag, duplicate/bowtie status, explicit unknown dimensions/support, radiance units, allocation group and all six source hashes. `TRIANGULAR_ANALYSIS.json` additionally retains every native sparse FP field, four nearest750m center candidates, the Aqua candidate and its own C6/C6.1 QA fields. `POSITIVE_EVIDENCE.csv` is the initial compact backend table; it is preserved separately. Decimal precision preserves stored values and does not imply corresponding physical measurement accuracy.','',
    '## FRP method and QA applicability','',
    'The [official C2 375m guide1.2](https://ladsweb.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/archive/Document%20Archive/Science%20Data%20Product%20Documentation/VIIRS_C2_AF-375m_User_Guide_1.2.pdf), Table2 and section3.1.3/Figure2, was visually reviewed from the exact local PDF, not interpreted from a misaligned text table. It describes M13-based fractional allocations among375m detections. Zero/null FRP can arise from unavailable retrievals, including saturation/background problems; it does not mean absent fire. No zero/null occurs in these sixteen records. Bit6 is M13 input quality, bit5 geolocation input quality, and bit22 residual bowtie; all are nominal/clear here. Table2 detection flags are exported separately from those input-quality bits.','',
    'The exact750m file is Collection002, NPP_PR14 1.6.1, PGE2.0.4, produced2023. The375m file is Collection002, NPP_PR14IMG3.1.6, PGE2.0.13, produced2024, with the same named M13 input. The difference in processing versions prevents attributing the observed contrast solely to resolution. Operational NRT documentation is not substituted for these Standard Processing products.','',
    'The [current official C2 CMR collection metadata](https://cmr.earthdata.nasa.gov/search/collections.umm_json?concept_id=C2545314536-LPCLOUD) still links the older `VNP14_User_Guide_V1.pdf` and the [Collection1 file specification](https://ladsweb.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/filespec/VIIRS/1/VNP14), which identifies NPP_PR14 V1.4.3, January2019. No authoritative applicability statement for SP NPP_PR14 1.6.1/PGE2.0.4 was obtained. The acquired algorithm-QA variable supplies only “bit field”, without flag_masks/flag_meanings. A375m decoder would interpret raw word2 as an I2-input warning, illustrating why it cannot be silently applied to750m. **Exact750m C2 QA remains WITHHELD.** The precise evidence and URLs are in `phase9/SOURCE_QUALIFICATION.json`; the search was bounded and stopped.','',
    '## Geometry, temporal checks and categories','',
    f"Nearest750m centers are {min(r['viirs750']['distance_m'] for r in pixels):.4f}–{max(r['viirs750']['distance_m'] for r in pixels):.4f}m away, with measured view zenith39.68–39.99°. All16 pass the frozen40° center-view screen, but none passes30°. Four-neighbor identities and distances reconcile independently; maximum numeric distance difference is {o['max_nearest_geodesic_difference_m']:.12g}m. Numerical agreement is not physical geolocation accuracy. All16 scan27 timing and orbit-midpoint checks agree between exact375m and750m geolocation inputs. No exact exposure timestamp, physical footprint boundary or response uncertainty was invented.",'',
    'Actual Aqua candidate center distances are154.947–787.100m. All have native mask5; their own Table4 QA is retained. The selected-candidate scan-separation bound is68.956359s. The unchanged Phase8 full-AOI bound remains75.16694808s: these refer to different scopes, not a retrospective threshold change. Correct source-specific QA and short timing alone do not qualify physical shared area. The inherited nominal MODIS IFOV stress test remains unqualified. No center-spacing polygons, GRings or10km occupied-cell-day overlap were substituted for observation opportunity.','',
    '| Requested category | Assigned rows |','|---|---:|']
    for category in c['categories']:lines.append(f"| {category} | {a['category_counts'].get(category,0)} |")
    lines+=['', 'These are category assignments, not sensitivity/specificity metrics. “Unmatched” is0 because temporal-compatible center candidates were found; physical containment remains unresolved. All16 remain UNKNOWN_SUPPORT because exact750m QA and physical response boundaries are unqualified. Qualified shared area:null; qualified disagreements:null; qualified matched positives:null; valid shared negative controls:null. Independent physical fire-absence controls:0. Phase8 southern raw non-fire-mask controls remain unchanged and unqualified.','',
    '## Baseline, candidate and uncertainty','',
    '| Stage | Actual result |','|---|---|','| B0 native | Preserved source-separated16/0/0 positive-mask result and allocated375m FRP |','| B1 common support | WITHHELD; area and qualified comparisons UNKNOWN |','| B2 within-VIIRS | Same named M13 input, identical scan bounds,12 allocation-consistent groups and16 nearby coarse mask5 centers independently verified; all16 support categories UNKNOWN |','| B3 Aqua/750m continuity | Candidate centers and bounded timing inspected; no qualified common domain |','| B4 combined historical estimand | NOT RELEASED |','',
    'No coefficient, correction factor, normalized sensor trend, missed-fire rate or anomaly was fitted. No improvement over an unchanged baseline was independently demonstrated. Sixteen enriched positives from one event/pass cannot meet the inherited30-qualified-pass/five-week floor; even the12 candidate allocation groups are spatially dependent and do not supply independent dates/events. No new model was preregistered because the prerequisite qualified evidence is absent. Original sealed holdouts, G4 bias/rank/corroboration/blocked-uncertainty conditions and required human signoffs remain intact. Generalization is untested; G4 stays ADJUSTMENT_WITHHELD.','',
    '## Actual application changes','',
    'A focused Triangular Bridge sits inside the existing Scientific Bridge laboratory. Selecting F01–F16 connects the375m native signal, nearest750m raw classification and Aqua candidate to five compact scientific answers. The map shows three exact centers and dashed candidate-association lines; it does not draw unqualified source footprints or the study box as coverage. Regional context is available without changing the scientific selection or export; it displays the original sixteen positive centers.','',
    'Selected CSV exports three source-center rows with source identities, raw QA, scan UTC, analysis/contract hashes, unqualified-support state and unchanged G4. A separate complete sixteen-row CSV exports the FRP/QA audit. Superseded mask requests retain the earlier abort protection. Native map/history/calendar and MemoryLoss remain usable; no dates, observation opportunities, physical fires or harmonized historical counts are filled. L2 distribution attribution now names NASA LP DAAC/LAADS/UMD when inspecting L2 evidence.','',
    'Rendered review found insufficient geographic context at native-center scale and excessive mobile card height. A context/detail toggle and compact mobile controls corrected these concrete issues. Expanded five-step evidence remains on demand; ordinary mobile view does not render long explanations across the map. The event calendar remains June2023 with the original857-record native context, separate from this current L2 production vintage.','',
    'Modified inherited source files:','']
    lines+=['- `'+name+'`' for name in p['modified']]
    lines+=['','New implementation/verification files:','']
    sources=['src/triangular.ts','src/TriangularBridge.tsx','science/phase9_contract.py','science/phase9_analysis.py','science/phase9_oracle.py','science/phase9_references.py','science/phase9_publish.py','science/phase9_memory.py','science/phase9_report.py','science/test_phase9.py','scripts/phase9-preserve.py','scripts/phase9-secret-check.py','scripts/phase9-review.mjs','tests/phase9.spec.ts']
    lines+=['- `'+name+'`' for name in sources]
    lines+=['', 'Research namespace: `public/data/phase9/p9-6bf2cedaf20f-8fce69a95ef1/`. No native/P6/P7/P8 pointer was replaced. Generated evidence is under `reports/phase9/`; exact source and modified-file hashes are recorded in its preservation manifest.','',
    '## Executed tests, screenshots and performance','',
    f"Scientific tests: **52/52 PASS** (`phase9/science-final-tests.log`). Final browser suite: **{t['stats']['expected']}/111 PASS**, {t['stats']['unexpected']} unexpected, {t['stats']['flaky']} flaky, {t['stats']['skipped']} skipped, {t['stats']['duration']/1000:.3f}s (`phase9/full-browser-results.json`). All original suites and eight Phase9 tests ran; coverage includes all16 selections and exported center identities, complete16-row UTC/QA/hash table, checksum withholding, regional/detail selection retention, rendered points and keyboard widths1440/390/320. Initial109-test results are preserved separately. Production TypeScript/Vite build PASS; inherited MapLibre chunk-size advisory remains.",'',
    f"Three fresh local production-preview contexts: median answer readiness {statistics.median(r['answerMs'] for r in v['runs'])}ms; evidence binding {statistics.median(r['bindMs'] for r in v['runs'])}ms; rendered geographic map {statistics.median(r['geographicMs'] for r in v['runs'])}ms. Selection switches {min(s['ms'] for r in v['runs'] for s in r['switches'])}–{max(s['ms'] for r in v['runs'] for s in r['switches'])}ms; median page-JS heap snapshot {statistics.median(r['heap_snapshot_bytes'] for r in v['runs'])/1e6:.2f}MB. Every capture rendered3 candidate centers from4 GeoJSON features; no footprint polygons and no page errors were captured.",'',
    f"Warm production replay {m['production_seconds']:.3f}s; independent raw-mask/scalar-geodesic replay {m['independent_seconds']:.3f}s; OS-reported Python peak working set {m['peak_working_set_bytes']/1e6:.2f}MB. These warm local replays recomputed and byte-checked immutable outputs after browser validation. Cached file reads are not cold acquisition throughput benchmarks. Browser JS snapshots exclude workers/GPU and are not peak memory. Provider/network basemap latency varies; DOM occlusion is not perceptual measurement.",'',
    '| Width×900 | Map / viewport | Compact unobscured map / viewport | Overflow |','|---|---:|---:|---|']
    for capture in v['captures']:
        r=capture['compact'];lines.append(f"| {capture['width']} | {r['map_viewport_fraction']*100:.1f}% | {r['unobscured_viewport_fraction']*100:.1f}% | none |")
    lines+=['', 'Mobile remains below 70% unobscured viewport; the card can expand/scroll on demand and the map still occupies 62.7% of the viewport. Close candidate views can have few geographic features in this forested tract. Regional context preserves the selection and reveals surrounding geography when detailed tiles are available. The final desktop capture used the coarse Natural Earth fallback, which cannot show local roads/lakes; mobile captures and all three timed contexts rendered detailed provider tiles. The small inherited basemap-status label partly overlaps the scale at the lower left. No horizontal page overflow was observed. Exact rendered screenshots were opened and reviewed: `screenshots/phase9-{result,map,context,evidence}-{1440,390,320}.png`; hashes and visual limitations are in `phase9/VISUAL_REVIEW.json`.','',
    '## Preservation and authorization','',
    f"Before-edit snapshot:1,076 files,11,257,713 bytes, SHA256 `daa85fd79e7008ae997f275f472ae5b8a63b22616237cc7552269faef8bb592c`. {p['inherited_unchanged']} inherited files byte-unchanged; five inherited UI files changed. All{len(p['immutable_checks'])} original archive/database and Phase6–8 payload checks passed. Prior scientific source, tests, reports, release identities, cohorts, original native quantities, holdouts and G4 files are preserved. New raw science payload bytes:0. No new Earthdata authentication or credential configuration was required. Secret-scan scope/results are recorded separately; no private token, account identifier, credential hash or signed redirect was exported.",'',
    'Local BUILD authorization remains USER-ATTESTED. Existing unresolved global-award/reuse eligibility has not been represented as verified NASA approval. No NASA endorsement, independent human science signoff or calibrated continuity is claimed.','',
    '## Approximately90-second judge demonstration','',
    'Open `http://127.0.0.1:5174/?region=canada&lab=1&study=phase9`.','',
    '**0–15s:** “MODIS and VIIRS observe fire activity differently. More detections do not automatically mean more physical fires or a longer calibrated history.”','',
    '**15–35s:** Select F02, then F03. “These are distinct375m detections with equal fractional FRP. Our raw-data recount finds16 pixels in12 allocation-consistent groups. Summing the native fractions once gives22.37MW; deleting equal fractions would be wrong.”','',
    '**35–55s:** Inspect on map, use regional context, then candidate centers. “The375m and750m products name the same M13 input and have identical scan intervals. Each nearby750m center is native class5. These are actual center positions, not invented fire perimeters or observation footprints.”','',
    '**55–75s:** Open five-step evidence. “The375m algorithm and separate750m product need not make the same detection decision. Exact750m C2 QA and physical containment remain unresolved. We therefore report UNKNOWN support, not missed fires or validated non-detections.”','',
    '**75–90s:** Export selected evidence and return to native history. “Every result retains UTC, QA and source hashes. The historical calendar remains useful and source-separated. We have proved a reproducible same-pass diagnostic and allocation distinction; harmonization and G4 remain withheld.”','',
    '## Next scientific milestone','',
    'Obtain an authoritative SP VNP14 C2 QA definition explicitly applicable to NPP_PR14 1.6.1/PGE2.0.4 and independently justified response footprints/registration uncertainty. Then classify physical shared support on this unchanged case. Only a separately preregistered, adequately replicated set of qualified dates/events could support fitting and independent validation; keep original holdouts sealed and never use an FRP coefficient as a hotspot-count factor.','']
    (ROOT/'reports/PHASE9_TRIANGULAR_BRIDGE_EXECUTION.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines),encoding='utf-8');print('reports/PHASE9_TRIANGULAR_BRIDGE_EXECUTION.md')
if __name__=='__main__':run()
